# Course title
The Software Engineering Revolution: Build Your Own SDD Framework Governed by Harness Principles
软件工程革命：基于 Harness 原则，构建自己的 SDD 框架

## Target audience

- Chief technology officers (CTOs)
- Leaders of AI-Powered Engineering Teams
- Software engineering leads
- Software engineers transitioning from traditional development or vibe coding to SDD and harness engineering

- 首席技术官（CTO）
- AI 赋能的工程团队负责人
- 软件工程团队负责人
- 希望从传统开发或 Vibe Coding 转向 SDD 和 Harness Engineering 的软件工程师

## Learning objectives (summary)

- Explain SDD, agentic programming, harness engineering, and their core concepts to establish a shared engineering vocabulary.
- Develop a simple application with skills to meet defined acceptance criteria.
- Create a RAG service and a local agent to provide answers grounded in retrieved sources through MCP.
- Design a Scrum-in-SDD framework to integrate team delivery practices with harness principles.
- Implement the framework on a RAG project to demonstrate incremental delivery, progress inspection, and continuous improvement.
- Design an organization-level framework outline to define shared standards and team responsibilities.


- 解释 SDD、智能体编程、Harness Engineering 及相关核心概念，建立统一的工程术语体系。
- 使用技能构建简单应用，使其满足明确的验收标准。
- 创建 RAG 服务和本地智能体，通过 MCP 提供有检索来源支持的回答。
- 设计融合 Scrum 的 SDD 框架，将团队交付实践与智能体运行约束原则相结合。
- 在 RAG 项目中实施该框架，实践增量交付、进度检查和持续改进。
- 设计组织级框架概要，明确共享标准与团队职责。

## Learning objectives

- Explain Spec-Driven Development (SDD), agentic programming, and harness engineering to distinguish their roles in guiding, executing, and controlling AI-assisted development.
- Explain the four SDD foundations—skills, rules, knowledge, and workflow—to assign each a clear responsibility in the development framework.
- Differentiate agents, Model Context Protocol (MCP), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and applications to map their roles in the class project.
- Develop a simple application using skills across acceptance-test-driven development (ATDD), UI design and mock-ups, technical design, implementation, and testing to meet defined acceptance criteria.
- Create a simple RAG solution exposed through an MCP service to answer questions using retrieved evidence and source citations.
- Create a custom local agent that calls the MCP service to complete a defined task within explicit operating limits.
- Design a Scrum-in-SDD framework using skills, rules, knowledge, and workflows to integrate Scrum and SDD under harness principles.
- Implement the Scrum-in-SDD framework while building the RAG MCP service to demonstrate backlog refinement, incremental delivery, progress inspection, and retrospectives.
- Design an organization-level framework outline to distinguish shared knowledge, rules, and services from team-specific workflows and backlogs.


- 解释规范驱动开发（SDD）、智能体编程和 Harness Engineering（智能体运行机制与约束设计），区分三者在指导、执行和约束 AI 辅助开发中的作用。
- 解释 SDD 的四项核心要素——技能、规则、知识和工作流，明确各自在开发框架中的职责。
- 区分智能体、模型上下文协议（MCP）、检索增强生成（RAG）和应用程序，明确它们在课程项目中的作用。
- 使用技能完成验收测试驱动开发（ATDD）、界面设计与原型制作、技术设计、编码实现和测试，构建符合验收标准的简单应用。
- 创建通过 MCP 服务提供功能的简单 RAG 方案，根据检索到的证据回答问题并标注来源。
- 创建能够调用 MCP 服务的本地定制智能体，在明确的运行边界内完成指定任务。
- 运用技能、规则、知识和工作流设计融合 Scrum 的 SDD 框架，使其遵循智能体运行约束原则。
- 在构建 RAG MCP 服务的过程中实施融合 Scrum 的 SDD 框架，实践待办事项梳理、增量交付、进度检查和回顾改进。
- 设计组织级框架概要，区分组织共享的知识、规则和服务，以及各团队自行管理的工作流和待办事项。

